<li><strong>Nubian goats produce</strong> less volume, but their milk is noticeably richer and sweeter. Many cheesemakers prefer them because more butterfat and protein means more cheese per gallon.</li>
<li><strong>Nigerian Dwarfs</strong> give the least milk by volume but the richest by far. For their size — 60 to 75 pounds — they are remarkably efficient.</li>
